list.item:
 Anderson, George W., Jr., Admiral, USN (ret.);
Chairman of the President’s Foreign Intelligence Advisory Board until
1976

 Armstrong, Anne L., Counselor to the President
from 1973 until 1974; U.S. Ambassador to the United Kingdom after March 17,
1976

 Buchen, Philip W., Executive Director, Domestic
Council Committee on the Right of Privacy from March until August 1974;
White House Counsel from August 15, 1974, until January 20, 1977

 Cranston, Alan, Senator (D–California);
Democratic Whip and Chairman, Senate Committee on Veterans’ Affairs from
January 1977

 Donaldson, William H., Under Secretary of State
for Security Assistance from November 26, 1973, until May 10, 1974;
thereafter Counsel to the Vice President

 Ford, Gerald R., member, U.S. House of
Representatives (R–Michigan) and Minority Leader until December 6, 1973;
thereafter Vice President of the United States until August 9, 1974;
thereafter President of the United States until January 20, 1977

 Harriman, W. Averell, Under Secretary of State
for Political Affairs from 1963 until 1965; Ambassador at Large; Chairman,
Foreign Policy Task Force, Democratic National Committee, 1976

 Holton, A. Linwood, Assistant Secretary of State
for Congressional Relations from February 28, 1974, until January 31,
1975

 Kubisch, Jack B., Assistant Secretary of State
for Inter-American Affairs from May 29, 1973, until September 4, 1974;
Ambassador to Greece from September 26, 1974

 Popper, David H., Assistant Secretary of State
for International Organization Affairs from July 12, 1973, until January 2,
1974; U.S. Ambassador to Chile from February 22, 1974

 Rockefeller, David, CEO, Chase Manhattan Bank;
member, Council of the Americas; Chairman, Council on Foreign
Relations

 Stennis, John C., Senator (D–Mississippi);
Chairman, Select Committee on Standards and Conduct until 1975; also
Chairman, Committee on Armed Services

 Stevenson, Adlai E., III, Senator (D–Illinois);
Chairman, Select Committee on the Senate Committee System from 1975 until
1976; also Chairman, Select Committee on Ethics from 1977

person.note:
Director, Policy Planning Staff, Department of Defense from 1973 until 1974;
                    Deputy Director, Policy Planning Staff, Department of State from 1974 until
                    1977

U.S. Permanent Representative to the United Nations until January 18, 1973;
                    Chairman of the Republican National Committee from 1973 until 1974; Head of the
                    U.S. Liaison Office in Beijing from October 21, 1974, until December 7, 1975;
                    Director of Central Intelligence from January 30, 1976, until January 20,
                    1977

Deputy Assistant to the President from December 1974 until November 1975;
                    White House Chief of Staff and Assistant to the President from November 1975
                    until January 1977

Assistant Secretary of State for East Asian and Pacific Affairs until May 10,
                    1973; U.S. Ambassador to Australia from March 27, 1973, until July 31, 1975;
                    also U.S. Ambassador to Nauru from February 28, 1974, until July 31, 1975

Under Secretary of State for Political Affairs from 1963 until 1965;
                    Ambassador at Large; Chairman, Foreign Policy Task Force, Democratic National
                    Committee, 1976

member, National Security Council Operations Staff/East Asia until March 1973;
                    co-Deputy Chief of Mission, U.S. Liaison Office in Beijing from 1973 until 1975;
                    U.S. Ambassador to Singapore from August 1975

U.S. Ambassador to Japan until November 8, 1973; Assistant Secretary of State
                    for East Asian and Pacific Affairs from January 8, 1974, until July 9, 1974;
                    Deputy Secretary of State from July 10, 1974, until March 31, 1976

Under Secretary of State for Political Affairs until February 1, 1973;
                    thereafter Ambassador at Large and head of the U.S. Delegation to the Strategic
                    Arms Limitation Talks

Counselor to the President from August 10, 1974, until January 20, 1977;
                    Chairman, White House Intelligence Coordination Group from 1975 until
                    1976
